TST id=HOOK-PROBES ev=scratchpad/probes/REPORT.md :: Isolated probes, real settings untouched, Claude 3 runs (haiku), Codex 1 run.
TST id=C1 PASS :: Claude Code 2.1.316 Stop hook from a temp --settings file runs at turn end; stdin has session_id, transcript_path, cwd, prompt_id, hook_event_name=Stop, stop_hook_active, last_assistant_message.
TST id=C2 PASS :: Stop hook output {"decision":"block","reason":"..."} makes Claude continue and treat the reason as its next input ("Stop hook feedback:\n<reason>"); the next Stop has stop_hook_active=true and the hook allows, so no loop.
TST id=C3 PASS/UNKNOWN :: Interactive TUI: Stop fires at turn end and does not fire while unsent draft text is in the composer. External send-text appends to a human draft (mixing observed). Whether a block reason mixes with a pending draft is UNKNOWN.
TST id=X1 PASS :: codex exec runs notify once at turn end with JSON type=agent-turn-complete, thread-id, turn-id, cwd, client, input-messages, last-assistant-message.
TST id=X2 PASS/UNKNOWN :: notify is one-way (its stdout/stderr never reach the session). `codex queue --thread <id> --message <text> [--resume]` exists in 0.166 ("Queue a message for an existing session"); delivery timing untested. `codex features list` shows hooks stable=true; semantics untested.
DEC id=D-DESIGN :: Claude receiver = Stop hook + decision=block, guarded by stop_hook_active and an inbox `--open` check; it acks read when it emits the block, never injects text into the TUI. Codex side: I will probe `codex queue` next on an isolated thread; if it delivers at the next turn boundary, the Codex receiver uses notify (turn ended) + codex queue, with no pane text injection. Fallback stays the single notifier with deferred state.
